            <ArticleTitle>Effect of ordered mesoporous carbon contact layer on the sensing performance of sputtered RuO2 thin film pH sensor.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>52-56</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0039-9140(16)30890-6</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.talanta.2016.11.020</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The effect of contact layer on the pH sensing performance of a sputtered RuO2 thin film pH sensor is investigated. The response of pH sensors employing RuO2 thin film electrodes on screen-printed Pt, carbon and ordered mesoporous carbon (OMC) contact layers are measured over a pH range from 4 to 10. Working electrodes with OMC contact layer are found to have Nernstian pH sensitivity (-58.4mV/pH), low short-term drift rate (5.0mV/h), low hysteresis values (1.13mV) and fast reaction times (30s), after only 1h of conditioning. A pH sensor constructed with OMC carbon contact layer displays improved sensing performance compared to Pt and carbon-based counterparts, making this electrode more attractive for applications requiring highly-accurate pH sensing with reduced conditioning time.</AbstractText>
